      "body": "## Motivation\n\n`TokenizerManager._create_tokenized_object` always runs `array(\"q\", input_ids)`, which walks the input and allocates a fresh int64 array for every request, even when the caller already holds a typecode-`q` array. Callers that receive token ids from a binary buffer (for example an Engine fed by an external router) currently pay for this second copy on every request.\n\n## Modifications\n\nPass `input_ids` through unchanged when it is already an `array` with typecode `\"q\"`. Lists, tuples, and arrays of any other typecode still go through the converting constructor, so existing callers see no change.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nNot applicable: no change to model forward or outputs.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNo benchmark included. The change only skips a redundant copy for callers that already hold an int64 array and is a no-op for all other callers.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [ ] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests). Covered by the existing Engine and server tests, which exercise the list path.\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\n- [ ] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed). See above.\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #35638312704](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/35638312704)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #35638312255](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/35638312255)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #35638312669](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/35638312669)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
